    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Table&nbsp;3.02</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> Spitz naevus subtypes</span></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "de la Fouchardière A and Gerami P",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.5pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Histological patterns</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; border-right: none; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-top: 1pt solid windowtext; background: #8db3e2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Clinical subtype</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>ALK</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{34761304;29635259}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Plexiform with elongated fascicles of spindle cells, myxoid, angiomatoid</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Often high mitotic counts and may have ulceration</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>ROS1</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{34761304;32862201;33004920}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Plexiform or plaque like, angiomatoid</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Highly characteristic features are floating nests in the epidermis, with transepidermal elimination of nests and pagetoid spread</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Eruptive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>NTRK1</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{27776007;30844834}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Filigree-like rete ridges, exaggerated maturation, (often) pigmentation, and predominantly spindle cell morphology are common; lobulated nesting pattern; rosettes; dysplastic naevus&ndash;like appearance</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>NTRK3</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{29794873;32968185}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><a name=\"_Hlk188518442\"></a><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PSCN appearance</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>BRAF</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{34761304;27776007}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Hyalinizing, dysplastic, often predominantly epithelioid</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>HRAS</em> mutations <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{23884457;25613920}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Desmoplastic</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Eruptive</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>PRKAR1A</em> inactivation as secondary event <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{35503882;35319526}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Pigmented epithelioid cell</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>MAP3K8</em> fusion <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{30640733}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Predominantly epithelioid and often highly pleomorphic, sometimes pigmented</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; background: #daeef3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 183.55pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"245\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Spitz naevus with <em>RET</em> fusions <span class=\"Ref-ID\" style=\"color: windowtext; border: none;\">{33742998}</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 412.25pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"550\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Plaque-type, sometimes with dyscohesive nesting</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 107.5pt; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-left: none; border-image: initial; border-bottom: 1pt solid windowtext; padding: 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"143\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">PSCN, pigmented spindle cell naevus.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Note: Specific molecular anomalies, particularly fusion genes in the MAPK pathway, appear to have a correlation with various histological patterns. However, it is important to note that multiple histological patterns may occur within the same tumour, and this may not necessarily indicate an exclusive genetic alteration.</span></p>",
